    "body": "## Summary\n- add an admin client for the read-only reactivation-audit endpoint\n- show per-account reactivation history on demand in the admin user list\n- refresh and expand the immutable audit immediately after a successful recovery\n- show acting administrator identity, status transition and timestamp newest-first\n- keep audit data out of public user surfaces and update account/access documentation\n\n## UX / privacy\nHistory is fetched lazily only when an administrator opens it, so the normal admin overview does not fan out into N+1 requests. The panel displays only the existing audit DTO: account/admin identifiers, administrator identity, status transition and timestamp. It does not expose location, escrow, route, job-private or payment data.\n\n## Validation\nRun frontend lint/build plus the existing API/runtime and identity gates. Do not merge unless required checks are green.",
